re/src/mutations.rs` violation.\n\nSecond known blemish, disclosed rather than hidden: four --symbol code references on this record (backfill_code_reference_ids, Store::update_code_reference, Store::remove_code_reference, and Command) are permanently SYMBOL-AMBIGUOUS under strata code-ref-check, for a different reason than EDR-0016''''''s SYMBOL-MISSING case. graphlite resolve <name> finds exactly one unambiguous candidate for each (verified directly), but cli/src/symbol_locator.rs evidently drives code-ref-check through graphlite''''''s broader symbols full-text search rather than its ranked resolve, and that search returns multiple hits for these names (e.g. backfill_code_reference_ids also matches the enclosing Store impl block''''''s text). This is a second, distinct gap between what graphlite can unambiguously answer and what code-ref-check actually asks it, on top of EDR-0016''''''s finding that const items are not indexed as symbols at all. As before, code_reference rows cannot be edited or deleted once ambiguity like this is discovered after the fact by the same tooling this record is about fixing -- so working path-plus-line-range references (no --symbol) were added alongside each broken one rather than replacing them. Net effect: five permanently broken code references now exist across EDR-0016 and EDR-0017 (one SYMBOL-MISSING, four SYMBOL-AMBIGUOUS), each with a working fallback beside it, and strata code-ref-check will report exactly these five findings going forward until graphlite''''''s symbol_locator integration is revisited -- not proposed by this record.","context":"EDR-0006 gave evidence a per-record identifier (`{record_id}-EV-{ordinal:03}`) but explicitly left code_reference out of scope, since at the time code_reference had no identifier column at all and no need for one -- it only supported creation. That gap became a real usability problem this session: a code reference was added to EDR-0016 with a `--symbol` argument that graphlite could not